# ShowMesh node agent environment template.
#
# install.sh copies this file to /etc/showmesh/agent.env (mode 0600,
# root:root) ONLY if that file does not already exist. It never
# overwrites a running node's configuration. Edit the installed copy, not
# this one, then `systemctl restart showmesh-agent`.
#
# The agent has no config file and no command-line flags: every setting
# is an environment variable, read once at process start
# (internal/agent/config/config.go). This file documents every variable
# that package recognizes as of this release. An unset variable takes the
# default named below.

# --- Identity (required to change from the default) ---

# SHOWMESH_NODE_ID identifies this node in every showmesh/nodes/<node-id>/...
# MQTT topic. Defaults to the OS hostname, but the hostname must already be
# a valid node id (lowercase letters, digits, internal hyphens only) or the
# agent refuses to start. Set this explicitly rather than relying on the
# hostname default. It MUST equal the username you provisioned with
# deploy/mosquitto/add-agent-credential.sh (see deploy/node/README.md).
# Reserved and rejected: coordinator, fpp, healthcheck.
SHOWMESH_NODE_ID=

# SHOWMESH_NODE_LABEL is an optional human-readable name shown alongside
# SHOWMESH_NODE_ID in the coordinator's inventory. Purely cosmetic.
#SHOWMESH_NODE_LABEL=

# --- Broker connection ---

# SHOWMESH_MQTT_BROKER is the broker URL. Default: tcp://localhost:1883
#SHOWMESH_MQTT_BROKER=tcp://localhost:1883

# SHOWMESH_MQTT_CLIENT_ID is the MQTT client id. Default:
# showmesh-agent-<node-id>. Change only if you need a specific value; two
# agents sharing a client id will kick each other off the broker.
#SHOWMESH_MQTT_CLIENT_ID=

# SHOWMESH_MQTT_USERNAME / SHOWMESH_MQTT_PASSWORD are this node's broker
# credentials, provisioned once with:
#   deploy/mosquitto/add-agent-credential.sh <node-id>
# Never commit real values here. Leave both empty only against a broker
# that still allows anonymous connections.
SHOWMESH_MQTT_USERNAME=
SHOWMESH_MQTT_PASSWORD=

# --- State and assets ---

# SHOWMESH_ASSET_DIR is where show assets (FSEQ, audio) are stored and
# played from, and where the agent's own durable state lives
# (.render-state/assignments.json, audio-sessions/*.json). It defaults to
# "./assets", relative to the process's working directory: a unit MUST
# set this explicitly, since systemd's WorkingDirectory alone is not a
# guarantee every future change to this unit preserves. install.sh points
# this at the systemd StateDirectory it creates.
SHOWMESH_ASSET_DIR=/var/lib/showmesh/assets

# --- Capabilities and logging ---

# SHOWMESH_NODE_CAPABILITIES overrides the capability set this agent
# advertises. Comma-separated "id" or "id:version" entries. Leave unset in
# production: there is no real capability-detection mechanism this
# overrides yet, so this exists for testing only.
#SHOWMESH_NODE_CAPABILITIES=

# SHOWMESH_LOG_LEVEL is one of debug|info|warn|error. Default: info
#SHOWMESH_LOG_LEVEL=info

# --- Optional GStreamer/tooling overrides ---
# Only needed when the binary isn't on PATH under its normal name, or you
# need to substitute a non-hardware sink for testing.

# SHOWMESH_GST_LAUNCH overrides the gst-launch-1.0 path (default: resolved
# from PATH).
#SHOWMESH_GST_LAUNCH=

# SHOWMESH_GST_DISCOVERER overrides the gst-discoverer-1.0 path (default:
# resolved from PATH).
#SHOWMESH_GST_DISCOVERER=

# SHOWMESH_GST_AUDIO_SINK_FACTORY substitutes a non-hardware GStreamer sink
# factory (e.g. "fakesink") for the production "alsasink". Test/bench only,
# never set this on a real node, or it will report success without
# opening a real audio device.
#SHOWMESH_GST_AUDIO_SINK_FACTORY=

# GST_PLUGIN_PATH: only needed on a render node that also needs the NDI
# output element (ndisink), which is NOT built or shipped by this repo
# (ADR-010 forbids shipping the NDI runtime; the gst-plugins-rs NDI
# element build is a separately owned recipe, see deploy/node/README.md).
# If you have built it by hand, point this at the directory containing
# libgstndi.so so GStreamer's registry can find it.
#GST_PLUGIN_PATH=

# --- Report cadence (advanced; defaults are fine for almost every node) ---

#SHOWMESH_ASSET_INVENTORY_INTERVAL=2m
#SHOWMESH_RENDER_REPORT_INTERVAL=15s
#SHOWMESH_AUDIO_REPORT_INTERVAL=15s

# --- MultiSync (render nodes only) ---

# SHOWMESH_MULTISYNC_LISTEN_ADDR overrides the local "host:port" the
# MultiSync listener binds. Default: ":32320" (FPP's fixed control port).
#SHOWMESH_MULTISYNC_LISTEN_ADDR=

# SHOWMESH_MULTISYNC_INTERFACE restricts the MultiSync multicast join to
# one named network interface. Default: join every suitable interface.
#SHOWMESH_MULTISYNC_INTERFACE=

# --- Node-local diagnostic idle output (render nodes only) ---
# This is the one render output that needs NOTHING else to be running: no
# coordinator, no broker, no FPP master, no assigned sequence. Set the
# surface variable and the node draws a moving diagnostic bar on it from
# the moment the agent starts, so "is anything reaching the projector"
# has an answer while the rest of the show is down. It never takes a
# surface a real assignment already owns.

# SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_SURFACE names the surface to draw it on.
# Empty (the default) disables the feature entirely.
#SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_SURFACE=

# Geometry and tick rate. Defaults: 1920x1080 at 40 fps. Setting any of
# these without SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_SURFACE is refused at startup
# rather than ignored.
#SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_WIDTH=1920
#SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_HEIGHT=1080
#SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_FRAME_RATE=40

# SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_NDI_SOURCE_NAME is the NDI source it sends
# on. Leave empty and the pipeline still runs, into a fakesink, and says
# so in its render report rather than claiming a working output.
#SHOWMESH_RENDER_DIAGNOSTIC_NDI_SOURCE_NAME=

# --- Read API authentication (only if the coordinator has closed
# anonymous reads; ADR-024) ---

#SHOWMESH_AGENT_API_TOKEN=
